Here's my question: is it possible to get a helm
of telepathy by polymorphing? And one more thing. Why are
elven shields _so_ bloody rare, seeing as they're absolutely
no particular use? 

OK, spoiler time now. How does one obtain large numbers of
spellbooks? (My news poster may eat "ctrl-L"'s so try not
to peek.)



Well, first, you need: a) ring of polymorph control b) ring of
polymorph c) wand of polymorph d) pick-axe (or force bolt).

Polymorphing a boulder gives a statue, which if done on a
sufficiently deep level gives a spellbook on breaking with
a pick-axe. Your local friendly dwarf/umber hulk/rock mole
will create large numbers of boulders at each dungeon lev.
Become a stone giant and go around gathering all the 
boulders you can find, and proceed in the above manner.

I believe this is a bug since (correct me if I'm wrong)
statues made by beating creatures with cockatrice corpses
or by creatures fighting your pet cockatrice won't ever
contain spellbooks. 

